{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q663902","formula":"C₄H₁₀O","hill":"C4H10O","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":4.0,"H":10.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Butanol","ru":"Бутанол","uk":"Бутиловий спирт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Butanol (also called butyl alcohol) is a four-carbon alcohol with a formula of C4H9OH, which occurs in five isomeric structures (four structural isomers), from a straight-chain primary alcohol to a branched-chain tertiary alcohol; all are a butyl or isobutyl group linked to a hydroxyl group (sometimes represented as BuOH, sec-BuOH, i-BuOH, and t-BuOH). These are 1-butanol, two stereoisomers of sec-butyl alcohol, isobutanol and tert-butyl alcohol. Butanol is primarily used as a solvent and as an intermediate in chemical synthesis, and may be used as a fuel.","ru":"Бутиловый спирт или бутанол (C4H9OH) — маслянистая, бесцветная жидкость с характерным запахом сивушного масла.","uk":"Бути́ловий спи́рт або бутано́л— 4 органічні сполуки з формулою C4H9OH. Безбарвні рідини (окрім трет-бутанолу, який є твердою речовиною) з характерним запахом сивушного масла."},"fame":45,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCO","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q15711994","names":{"en":"group of isomeric entities","ru":"семейство химических соединений","uk":"родина хімічних сполук"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":null,"atoms":15,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.51,"y":0.691,"z":0.379,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.633,"y":-0.507,"z":0.708,"el":"C"},{"x":0.295,"y":-0.918,"z":-0.438,"el":"C"},{"x":1.305,"y":0.143,"z":-0.862,"el":"C"},{"x":2.167,"y":0.488,"z":0.213,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.084,"y":0.518,"z":-0.537,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.219,"y":0.873,"z":1.193,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.915,"y":1.599,"z":0.249,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.282,"y":-1.358,"z":0.948,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.051,"y":-0.296,"z":1.613,"el":"H"},{"x":0.843,"y":-1.812,"z":-0.115,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.307,"y":-1.